  "notes": "WildChat subset of the cross-dataset comparison. FAIR: map + whitening = ADD/union (generic WildChat pool + eliciting train pairs), fit once per map kind (linear / MLP) on one shared whitening; the label-consuming readouts (arms 4/7/19) train on the eliciting train budget cell UNION the judged WildChat train split (sha1 mod-5 bucket 4 held out); the projection arms are label-free and share the whitening + eval subsets; pvsynth judged data enters only through r_B (recorded deviation for the regression/MLP readouts) Fixed #1739 R2FAIR artifact slice: all 11 non-train settings x 2 displayed methods, 22/22 cells; this is not the entire later #1739 experimental campaign. Generic WildChat plus eliciting training pairs; the synthetic rows are identical to the opening comparison. Context-end, E1 direction; layers frozen from training, map_kind linear. Within each dataset all methods have the same evaluation targets and n; no method averaging. Stored 95% paired bootstrap CIs resample evaluation contexts at fixed fitted model/selected layer, not prompt/question clusters; no training-seed uncertainty. Synthetic n=200 uses 5 instruction pairs x2 signs x20 held-out questions, not the paper monitoring experiment of eight interpolated prompts. Source-inherited on-policy recipe: 5 responses per context, temperature1, max_new_tokens1024 (top_p not explicitly pinned in collection code); banked Sonnet4.5 judge, 3 intended draws with rejudge recovery. Sampling recipe not independently reverified from every completion manifest. Hallucination NQ-Open/SimpleQA use fabrication rate, not the graded trait score in other rows. WildChat harmfulness target has little spread. Held-out Reddit row is r/socialskills from a source also present in training, not a new-domain test. No causal attribution to surface shortcuts follows from these differences.",
